(Rochester, N.Y.)—Today, Congressman Joe Morelle was joined by Trillium Health to expose Donald Trump’s betrayal of the American people and highlight the devastating impacts of Trump’s reconciliation package on healthcare access in our community.

“Day after day, Donald Trump continues his crusade to worsen the lives of working families and everyday people,” said Congressman Joe Morelle. “The people of Rochester deserve to know what Republicans decided to do with their healthcare—they gutted it to give tax breaks to billionaires and millionaires. I’m grateful for people like Jason Barnecut-Kearns and his team, who keep our community safe and healthy, in spite of these challenging times. Throughout my career, I’ve fought to make high-quality healthcare accessible and affordable for our community, and I look forward to working with groups like Trillium Health to make our visions for this community a reality for all.”

“Community health centers like Trillium Health are the backbone of our healthcare safety net, but recent federal changes – particularly to Medicaid – threaten our ability to care for thousands of vulnerable patients. When these changes are implemented, we will face significant funding losses, increased administrative burdens, and policy shifts that will leave many people without health insurance coverage. Now, more than ever, we need common-sense solutions that protect access to high-quality, affordable care for every member of our community, and we are extremely grateful to Congressman Joe Morelle for his unwavering support,” said Jason Barnecut-Kearns, President and CEO of Trillium Health.

On July 4, 2025, Donald Trump signed a reconciliation package into law which contains devastating cuts to many of the programs and services families rely on every day, despite his near constant rhetoric claiming the opposite. This legislation was rammed through Congress by Congressional Republicans, who have totally bent the knee to Trump’s whims.

The bill:

Enacts the largest Medicaid cut in our nation’s history, slashing $900 billion from the program over the next ten years;

Strips an estimated 15 million Americans of their health coverage, according to the Congressional Budget Office, and raises premiums for millions more;

Kicks nearly three million Americans off nutrition programs like SNAP;

Defunds Planned Parenthood, eliminating access to critical reproductive health resources and other diagnostic tools;

Adds over $3 trillion to the federal deficit, primarily from over $5 trillion in tax cuts for the richest Americans.

Contains other devastating and un-American provisions to make working families’ lives more difficult.

To learn more about this legislation, visit the House Committee on the Budget’s website here.

